          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The original independent-spin heat family can now be excluded at every nonnegative elapsed heat time, including times tending to infinity. The key is to roll back a fixed positive amount of heat and apply Lee–Yang together with Rodgers–Tao. A separate argument from Newman’s classical classification also excludes the stable Bessel control in the diverging-time regime, confirming that this is a limit of the construction family."
            ]
          },
